      "location": "Definition, admissible continuation chain condition",
      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "The definition requires only that successive elements be direct continuations; direct continuation is defined in def-function-element-and-direct-analytic-continuation by agreement “at a point a in U intersection V,” not at the joining path point. Take Omega=C×, V the plane slit along the nonpositive real ray with principal logarithm g, U the plane slit along the nonnegative real ray with the logarithm branch h having argument in (0,2pi), and gamma constantly -i. g and h agree at i, so the two-element chain is admitted, but g(-i)=-pi i/2 while h(-i)=3pi i/2. The missing agreement at gamma(t_j) permits a jump unrelated to the path.",
